    <Options>
      <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
        <Vermiculite code="3">
          <English>No Vermiculite</English>
          <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
        </Vermiculite>
      </Main>
      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>A $5,000 Good Energy air sealing rebate is available if you reduce air leakage from 3 or more air changes to 1.5 air changes or less (@50Pa). This can be achieved through a deep energy retrofit with comprehensive air sealing details performed on walls, ceilings and all building penetrations. Houses with low levels of air leakage require a balanced ventilation system, such as a heat recovery ventilator (HRV), to provide fresh air to the home and to exhaust stale air. See ventilation system comments for Good Energy HRV rebates.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Up to $12,000 in a Good Energy insulation rebate for above-grade walls is available if you add at minimum one times the existing wall insulation to the exterior of all above-grade walls. Consider adding two times the existing wall insulation to exterior walls for a more robust wall system that reduces the potential for moisture condensation. Adding two times the existing wall insulation can be an effective strategy for 2x4 walls but may not be as feasible or cost-effective for 2x6 or deeper wall systems.  </mainWalls>
                <foundation>Up to $10,000 in a Good Energy insulation rebate for below-grade walls is available if you add R20 or greater to all below-grade walls. The insulation in the below-grade wall system must be R20 or less prior to the retrofit. The rebate is proportional to the depth of the wall below grade. Walls that are 6 feet below-grade or deeper are eligible for the full rebate amount. A wall that is 3 feet below-grade is eligible for 50% of the rebate. 

</foundation>
                <windows>Up to $1,800 in a Good Energy windows rebate is available for upgrading your windows to ENERGY STAR units. You receive $120 per Energy STAR window upgrade to a maximum of $1,800 or 15 window replacements. You must provide ENERGY STAR documentation for each window installed. Sealed or insulated glass window units are not eligible for this rebate.</windows>
                <AdditionalComments>Programs in your region that you may be eligible for include: 
Good Energy rebates Â https://yukon.ca/en/buildings-and-homes
Better Buildings Program Â https://yukon.ca/en/housing-and-property/home-energy-rebates/get-funding-complete-residential-or-commercial-building
</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
      <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
        <Community>N/A</Community>
      </GreenerHomes>
